NiteWatch — Third-Party Data Notices
====================================

NiteWatch matches network destinations against public threat-intelligence data
that is downloaded to, and cached on, the user's own machine. The following
notices are required by the terms under which that data is provided, and must
be reproduced in product documentation and in any "About"/legal screen.

See docs/feed-licensing.md for the full per-source licensing analysis.

The notices below, together with the copyright and licence terms for NiteWatch
itself and for every third-party component, are reproduced in
agent/internal/help/licenses.md, which is compiled into the binary and shown in
the dashboard. That embedded copy is the one that satisfies these requirements
for a user holding only the executable; this file is its source-tree twin.


